"""
Grapheme clusters, the characters a reader sees, by the rules of Unicode's Standard Annex 29.

- The rules are those of Unicode version 17.0.0.
- An e with a combining acute is one cluster, and so is a flag of two regional indicators.
- Emoji joined by zero width joiners, a Hangul syllable in parts and a Devanagari conjunct are one.
- CR and LF together are one cluster.
- Text is UTF-8; a byte that does not begin well-formed UTF-8 ends the cluster before it.
- The display width is the count of columns a terminal shows: two for the wide and fullwidth East Asian classes and the emoji shown as emoji, none for combining marks and control characters, one otherwise.
- Truncation and wrapping cut at the ends of clusters and never inside one: fittingEnd gives the longest prefix of a width, lineEnd and countLines wrap the text into lines of a width.

    let clusters: Option[Index] := countClusters(asSpan(&name));
    let first_end: Option[Index] := clusterEnd(asSpan(&name), 0);
    let columns: Option[Index] := countColumns(asSpan(&name));
    let cut: Option[Index] := fittingEnd(asSpan(&name), 20);
"""
pragma Targets(Names => "linux openbsd freebsd darwin wasm");
module Standard.Grapheme is
    """
    The end of the grapheme cluster that starts at the byte start of text:
    the index of the byte after it, or the length of the text.  None when
    start is not below the length of the text, or no well-formed UTF-8
    begins at start.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function clusterEnd(text: Span[Nat8, R], start: Index): Option[Index];

    """
    The number of grapheme clusters of the text; 0 for the empty text.
    None when the text is not well-formed UTF-8.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function countClusters(text: Span[Nat8, R]): Option[Index];

    """
    The width in columns a terminal shows for the code point on its own:
    0, 1 or 2.  None for the combining marks, the control and format
    characters and the separators; two for the wide and fullwidth classes
    of East Asian Width and for the characters a terminal shows as emoji;
    one otherwise, the ambiguous classes among them, ambiguous counted
    narrow.
    """
    function pointWidth(point: Index): Index
        ensures result <= 2;

    """
    The width in columns of the cluster that starts at the byte start of
    text, the cluster walked as one: as wide as its first code point of a
    width above 0, two columns for a flag of two regional indicators and
    for a cluster that the variation selector 16 shows as emoji, one for
    a cluster that the variation selector 15 shows as text.  None when
    start is not below the length of the text, or no well-formed UTF-8
    begins at start.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function clusterWidth(text: Span[Nat8, R], start: Index): Option[Index];

    """
    The width in columns of the whole text, cluster by cluster; 0 for the
    empty text.  None when the text is not well-formed UTF-8.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function countColumns(text: Span[Nat8, R]): Option[Index];

    """
    The end of the longest prefix of the text that is at most width
    columns wide, always the end of a cluster: the index of the byte
    after it.  A prefix that would begin with a cluster wider than width
    stays empty.  None when the text is not well-formed UTF-8.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function fittingEnd(text: Span[Nat8, R], width: Index): Option[Index];

    """
    The end of the line that starts at the byte start of text, when every
    line holds clusters of at most width columns: the index of the byte
    after its last cluster.  The line breaks before a cluster that would
    not fit, and before a cluster of a carriage return or a line feed,
    which the line does not hold; a line holds at least one cluster.  The
    next line starts at this end, or, when a carriage return or a line
    feed stands there, after that cluster.  None when start is not below
    the length of the text, or no well-formed UTF-8 begins at start.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function lineEnd(text: Span[Nat8, R], width: Index, start: Index): Option[Index];

    """
    The number of lines the text wraps into at width columns a line, by
    the rules of lineEnd; 0 for the empty text.  None when the text is
    not well-formed UTF-8.
    No contract: an Option result, which an ensures cannot look into.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function countLines(text: Span[Nat8, R], width: Index): Option[Index];
end module.
